   <h3> Bloodhorde Membership</h3>
   <p>
   
<blockquote>
<p>We accept :</p>
<ol>
  <li>any class from the Dark Elf, Troll, Ogre, or Iksar races</li>
  <li>Shadow Knights and Necros from any race</li>
  <li>Clerics of Cazic Thule or Bertoxxulus religions</li>
  <li>Characters must be of at least level 24</li>
</ol>
<p>If your character falls within those basic guidelines, you must contact one 
  of the guild recruiters concerning your desired 
  membership. </p>
<p>If your character does not fall within those guidelines, we will not accept 
  you. Bloodhorde is a role-play evil-only guild. Many of our members are in Bloodhorde 
  for the main purpose that they can role-play evil. If we were to allow non-evil 
  characters within the guild, we would severely disrupt the overall role-play 
  environment for our members. If you really want to be in Bloodhorde, you need 
  a character that fits those guidelines. We suggest starting a new character. 
  Getting to lvl 24 doesn't take nearly as long as you think. Note that Bloodhorde 
  will not offer any &quot;power leveling&quot; services. An individual member 
  may offer to help, but the guild overall will <b>not</b> promise anything of 
  that nature.</p>

<p>If you are granted membership, you will be initiated as a minion of
Bloodhorde.  The minion rank is essentially a trial period.  This trial
period will last for 21 days.  After this time is up, Horde Members are
allowed to cast dissenting votes against the Minion if they feel the Minion
is not worthy of full membership and discuss the reasons with officers.
If a Minion receives one valid dissenting vote, they will be disbanded from
the guild.  The 21 trial days can be shorter or longer based on special
individual cases.
</blockquote>


